  "warnings": [],
  "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt examines the fundamental distinctions and historical shifts among the three activities of the vita activa—labor, work, and action—focusing in these chapters on how the rise of the animal laborans and modern utilitarianism have transformed society into a labor-and-consumption-driven culture that threatens the durability of the human world."
}
